module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.FlatCoproductRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FiniteHilbert.HilbertCoverMorSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FiniteHilbert.HilbertCoverPullbackFiber
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.IsStackFromRepresentableDiagonal
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.EffectiveDescentRefinement

/-!
# Effective descent in `ℋ_d` is a question about affine covering families

Condition (3) of **Stacks 026F** for the category `ℋ_d` of degree-`d` finite locally free covers
quantifies over every covering sieve of the big fppf site of `S`.  Effectivity is local on the
base, so it may be checked at a covering *refinement* of each sieve
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.hasEffectiveDescent_of_familyRefinements`), and the refinement may be
chosen in whatever class is convenient.  This file performs that choice for `ℋ_d` and discharges
every hypothesis of the reduction except the geometry.

Two inputs make the reduction unconditional where it is otherwise carried.  The sheaf condition
the reduction asks for — condition (2) of Stacks 026F — is proved for `ℋ_d` as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isMorSheaf_finiteCoverFibered`, so nothing of it has to be assumed.  And
the refinement itself is proved: through every point of the base of a covering sieve there passes
an arrow of the sieve with *affine* source, flat and locally of finite presentation, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_affine_flat_mem_sieve_of_mem_topology`, and the family of
those arrows indexed by the points of the base is jointly surjective, hence generates a covering
sieve by `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_flat_lfp`.

What is left is one geometric statement about one shape of covering family: a descent datum for
`ℋ_d` relative to the sieve generated by a jointly surjective family of flat morphisms locally of
finite presentation with affine sources is effective.  That is the hypothesis `heff` below, and
producing it is descent of finite locally free covers along an affine fppf covering.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.hasEffectiveDescent_finiteCoverProjection_of_affineRefinements`:
  condition (3) of Stacks 026F for `ℋ_d`, from effectivity relative to the sieves generated by
  jointly surjective flat families locally of finite presentation with affine sources.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isStack_finiteCoverFibered_of_affineRefinements` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isStackInGroupoids_finiteCoverFibered_of_affineRefinements`: the same
  hypothesis gives `ℋ_d` as a stack and as a stack in groupoids, the diagonal clause being
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.hasRepresentableDiagonal_finiteCoverFibered`.

## Implementation notes

The index type of the refining family is the type of points of the base, which is the only index
type available: the arrow of the sieve through a point is chosen point by point.  It lies in
`Type u`, and the index universe of
`CategoryTheory.Functor.hasEffectiveDescent_of_familyRefinements` is free, because
`CategoryTheory.Functor.HasEffectiveDescent` quantifies over sieves and so carries no index type.

No size bound on the family is used and no coproduct is formed.  The refinement is used as a
*family*, not collapsed to the single morphism out of the coproduct of its sources that
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_flat_singleton_refinement_of_mem_topology` provides; the
coproduct is what a one-morphism descent argument needs, and a family-indexed one does not pay
for it.

No tag attribute sits on anything here.  Condition (3) of Stacks 026F is not proved — it is
reduced — and conditions (1), (2) and (3) together are what Stacks 026F asserts.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 026F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/026F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02ZI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02ZI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05YQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05YQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S) (d : ℕ)

/-- Effectivity of the descent data of `ℋ_d` relative to the sieve generated by a jointly
surjective family of flat morphisms locally of finite presentation with affine sources.  This is
the one geometric input the reduction below consumes. -/
def AffineFamilyEffectiveDescent : Prop :=
  ∀ (T : BigFppfOver B S hS) (ι : Type u) (X : ι → BigFppfOver B S hS) (g : ∀ i, X i ⟶ T),
    (∀ i, IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (X i))) →
    (∀ i, Flat ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (g i))) →
    (∀ i, LocallyOfFinitePresentation ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (g i))) →
    (∀ x : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T,
      ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (g i))) →
    ∀ D : (finiteCoverProjection (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (d := d)).SieveDescentDatum
      (Sieve.ofArrows X g), D.IsEffective

/-- **Condition (3) of Stacks 026F for the category of degree-`d` finite locally free covers,
reduced to affine covering families.**  Every descent datum of `ℋ_d` relative to every covering
sieve of the big fppf site of `S` is effective as soon as the data relative to the sieves
generated by jointly surjective flat families locally of finite presentation with affine sources
are.

Effectivity may be checked at a covering refinement,
`CategoryTheory.Functor.hasEffectiveDescent_of_familyRefinements`, whose sheaf hypothesis is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isMorSheaf_finiteCoverFibered`.  The refinement taken is the family of
arrows of the sieve with affine source running through the points of the base, which exists by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_affine_flat_mem_sieve_of_mem_topology` and is a covering by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_flat_lfp`. -/
theorem hasEffectiveDescent_finiteCoverProjection_of_affineRefinements
    (heff : AffineFamilyEffectiveDescent B S hS d) :
    (finiteCoverProjection (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (d := d)).HasEffectiveDescent
      (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) := by
  classical
  refine Functor.hasEffectiveDescent_of_familyRefinements.{u}
    (isMorSheaf_finiteCoverFibered B S hS d) ?_
  intro T R hR
  choose X g hgR hgaff _hgsize hgf hgp hgcov using
    fun x => BigFppfOver.exists_affine_flat_mem_sieve_of_mem_topology B S hS hR x
  refine ⟨(BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T, X, g, hgR,
    BigFppfOver.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_flat_lfp B S hS X g (fun x => ⟨x, hgcov x⟩) hgf hgp,
    heff T _ X g hgaff hgf hgp fun x => ⟨x, hgcov x⟩⟩

/-- **The category of degree-`d` finite locally free covers is a stack, reduced to affine
covering families.**  Its diagonal is representable by algebraic spaces,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.hasRepresentableDiagonal_finiteCoverFibered`, so by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isStack_of_hasRepresentableDiagonal` the only clause left is the
effectivity of descent data, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.hasEffectiveDescent_finiteCoverProjection_of_affineRefinements`
supplies. -/
theorem isStack_finiteCoverFibered_of_affineRefinements
    (heff : AffineFamilyEffectiveDescent B S hS d) :
    (finiteCoverFibered B S hS d).val.p.IsStack (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) :=
  isStack_of_hasRepresentableDiagonal B S hS (finiteCoverFibered B S hS d)
    (hasRepresentableDiagonal_finiteCoverFibered B S hS d)
    (hasEffectiveDescent_finiteCoverProjection_of_affineRefinements B S hS d heff)

/-- **The category of degree-`d` finite locally free covers is a stack in groupoids, reduced to
affine covering families.**  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isStack_finiteCoverFibered_of_affineRefinements` followed by the
implication (3) ⟹ (1) of Stacks 02ZJ. -/
theorem isStackInGroupoids_finiteCoverFibered_of_affineRefinements
    (heff : AffineFamilyEffectiveDescent B S hS d) :
    (finiteCoverFibered B S hS d).val.p.IsStackInGroupoids.{w} (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) :=
  isStackInGroupoids_of_hasRepresentableDiagonal B S hS (finiteCoverFibered B S hS d)
    (hasRepresentableDiagonal_finiteCoverFibered B S hS d)
    (hasEffectiveDescent_finiteCoverProjection_of_affineRefinements B S hS d heff)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

end
